  "info": {
    "description": "The auth-server routes a Putnami workload calls with its own identity: RFC 8693 token exchange, API keys, bounded delegations, cache-write and dependency-read leases, identity-outbox control, and the operator reader and executor surfaces. Consumers call them through the generated client in clients/go. The OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect legs this server also serves are owned by their standards and are not in this document.",
    "title": "Putnami Auth Server",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
